  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Veil-render, Seciae~ is a Nightshelf hero of mythic standing who emerged during the Great Thaw, led the colony of ☽'scar Ramtatus~ through the Faction Wars, and survives into the Frozen Peace — a fact that distinguishes them from most figures of comparable reputation. They are a practitioner of ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, the time-fracturing ice-magic discovered by Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss at The Veil Vents, and the longest-attested holder of the ☽'micseleia' Dagger, a fire-core shadow-steel blade they are credited with forging during the Clever Ice Age. The dagger's provenance register records no other bearer who carried it as long.
    
    Their left flipper bears permanent scarring. The earliest account attributes this to bare-handed contact with fire-cores — "either in desperation or punishment" — while later sources amend the cause to Fissure☽ Aurora backlash, described as holding two forces apart with flesh alone. Both explanations circulate. Neither invites inquiry.
    
    ## Career
    
    In ☽'scar Ramtatus~'s founding years, Seciae~ was among the first practitioners of Fissure☽ Aurora, a technique combining aurora-crystals with fire-cores to produce self-sustaining light and heat. They demonstrated the method for Alnae~ Oss and the guild-masters, who recognized its potential to reduce Nightshelf dependence on the Flipper Accord's trade provisions. The relationship with Alnae~ Oss appears to have been instructional in both directions — Seciae~ demonstrated fire-crystal fusion while Alnae~ Oss provided foundational training in crystalline magic.
    
    Seciae~ was also among the first to detect corruption resurging near Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius, the deep marker-site, after sanctification rites had supposedly driven it back. The warning went largely unheeded. They later attempted to cleanse corruption from The Fissured Smelt~'s eastern wall — the same wall later breached by the Wake-Singers — but the blackness persisted despite their efforts.
    
    ## Present
    
    Seciae~ now resides in ☽'scar Ramtatus~'s lower caverns, moving with deliberate slowness, wrapped in charcoal cloth layered thick enough to muffle sound. The ☽'micseleia' Dagger hangs at their hip in an ancestor-bone sheath; they permit no one else to touch it. The blade carries an irreparable fracture from the Orca Incursion that widens with each use.
    
    They have never visited Vestigium∴moria, the memorial erected in their name in the deep tunnels to preserve the cost of their victories. ☽'Lucatransiius Glow-bringer, their oldest companion from the Thaw years, still leaves fire-tea at their door. It goes cold. Seciae~ drinks it anyway, the next morning, when no one is watching.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771574416253_0", anchor: "the longest-attested holder of the ☽'micseleia' Dagger, a fire-core shadow-steel blade they are credited with forging during the Clever Ice Age", text: "Seciae~ 'emerged during the Great Thaw.' Seciae~ forged the dagger 'during the Clever Ice Age.' These two claims sit three sentences apart and nobody — myself included, until this very pass — blinked at the contradiction. The Clever Ice Age predates the Great Thaw by generations at minimum. Either the forging attribution is false and the dagger is older than its supposed maker, or the emergence dating is wrong and Seciae~ is far more ancient than any other source attests. The deep ice at ☽'scar Ramtatus~ carries impressions of the dagger that predate impressions of Seciae~ by at least two readable strata. I let both claims stand in the main text because the provenance register asserts both. The provenance register is wrong about at least one of them.", type: :temporal, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771574416253_1", anchor: "recognized its potential to reduce Nightshelf dependence on the Flipper Accord's trade provisions", text: "Interesting that the guild-masters 'recognized its potential' and then did nothing visible with it for decades. The second and third secret drafts of the Flipper Accord — which I recovered from administrative ice and which no one has requested to see — contain explicit provisions banning dual-source energy techniques in trade-adjacent settlements. Someone recognized the potential. Someone else made sure it stayed potential.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771574416253_2", anchor: "The dagger's provenance register records no other bearer who carried it as long", text: "The provenance register has three unattributed gaps totaling roughly forty years. 'No other bearer who carried it as long' means 'no other bearer whose name was written down.'", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771574416253_3", anchor: "The warning went largely unheeded", text: "It was heeded. It was overruled. There is a difference, and the difference matters to the forty-six penguins who signed a petition demanding action at Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius before the breach. Their names are in the ice. 'Unheeded' erases them.", type: :correction, display: :popout
